From: fexdroid
Subject: [PATCH] JIT: carry invert without FlagM goes through the CarryInvert op

FEX keeps the x86 carry inverted in host NZCV.C and puts it back in the
canonical polarity before a carry read and at block exits. With FlagM that is
the CarryInvert IR op (cfinv). Without FlagM (Snapdragon 888 / Cortex-X1,
ARMv8.2) RectifyCarryInvert emitted LoadNZCV + Xor(1 << 29) + StoreNZCV
instead. The dead flag pass cannot remove that StoreNZCV when N or Z are still
live (test + je), so mrs/eor/msr stayed after test/and/or with an immediate or
an 8-bit test r,r even when nothing reads C afterwards.

RectifyCarryInvert now emits CarryInvert whenever NZCV is not dirty in a GPR,
on every host. The dead flag pass already treats it as reads C / writes C /
eliminable, so it disappears when C is dead. When C is live it is lowered to
mrs/eor/msr through TMP1 on hosts without FlagM (cfinv with FlagM, as
before). When NZCV is already loaded or dirty in a GPR the old GPR path is
kept, since inverting that copy is cheaper.

InstCountCI with FlagM disabled: test eax,0x10 / test rax,imm / and / test
al,al followed by je/jne whose successors overwrite the flags go from 7 to 4
host instructions; cases where adc/jb/setc read C keep the invert.

Local patch, not upstream.
---
diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/ALUOps.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/ALUOps.cpp
index 3691bca..9a00c29 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/ALUOps.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/ALUOps.cpp
@@ -285,8 +285,15 @@ DEF_OP(CmpPairZ) {
 }
 
 DEF_OP(CarryInvert) {
-  LOGMAN_THROW_A_FMT(CTX->HostFeatures.SupportsFlagM, "Unsupported flagm op");
-  cfinv();
+  if (CTX->HostFeatures.SupportsFlagM) {
+    cfinv();
+  } else {
+    // No FlagM: flip C (NZCV bit 29) through the scratch register. TMP1 is
+    // never allocated and this op has no register sources.
+    mrs(TMP1, ARMEmitter::SystemRegister::NZCV);
+    eor(ARMEmitter::Size::i32Bit, TMP1, TMP1, 1u << 29);
+    msr(ARMEmitter::SystemRegister::NZCV, TMP1);
+  }
 }
 
 DEF_OP(RmifNZCV) {
diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher.h b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher.h
index 3b97045..9bfca9b 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher.h
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher.h
@@ -1778,8 +1778,13 @@ private:
   // operation reading carry or at the end of a block.
   void RectifyCarryInvert(bool RequiredInvert) {
     if (CFInverted != RequiredInvert) {
-      if (CTX->HostFeatures.SupportsFlagM && !NZCVDirty) {
-        // Invert as NZCV.
+      if (!NZCVDirty && (CTX->HostFeatures.SupportsFlagM || !CachedNZCV)) {
+        // Invert as NZCV. This is a single cfinv with FlagM, and mrs/eor/msr
+        // through a scratch register without it. Either way it stays a
+        // CarryInvert op in the IR, which the dead flag pass removes when the
+        // carry is not read afterwards (e.g. test + je, or a block exit with
+        // the flags dead). Without FlagM, if NZCV is already loaded into a
+        // GPR, inverting that copy saves the mrs, so keep doing that.
         _CarryInvert();
         CachedNZCV = nullptr;
       } else {
diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/IR/IR.json b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/IR/IR.json
index fc5d0aa..1712704 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/IR/IR.json
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/IR/IR.json
@@ -1149,7 +1149,7 @@
         ]
       },
       "CarryInvert": {
-        "Desc": ["Invert carry flag in NZCV"],
+        "Desc": ["Invert carry flag in NZCV", "cfinv with FlagM, else mrs/eor/msr through a scratch register"],
         "HasSideEffects": true
       },
       "AXFlag GPR:$V_inv": {
